            789
          ]
        }
      ],
      "finding": "Bool participates in the integral sum kernel. Each scalar addition returns Bool; generic vector addition stores each lane back into Bool. On canonical 0/1 values this operation is logical OR, with false identity. The fetched x86 vector headers have no Bool arithmetic specialization replacing this rule."
    },
    {
      "id": "empty-reduction",
      "sources": [
        {
          "path": "aten/src/ATen/native/ReduceOps.cpp",
          "lines": [
            1297,
            1300
          ]
        },
        {
          "path": "aten/src/ATen/native/cpu/Reduce.h",
          "lines": [
            251,
            260
          ]
        }
      ],
      "finding": "The empty reduction path zeros the result; nonempty reduction initializes its Bool result with the zero identity. Empty result shapes remain empty. New output Version must be observed in the new reference; this source review assigns no oracle Version."
    },
